 "notes": "Observed 95% power-constrained upper limit on |g_agamma| from the fiducial NuSTAR M82 analysis (black solid curve with green/yellow expected band in Fig. 2 of the paper), extracted from the vector PDF fig2_041924.pdf in the e-print. M82 is the paper's headline/strongest result (|g|<6.4e-13 GeV^-1 for m_a<1e-10 eV; the M87 analysis gives the weaker 8.4e-13). Axis calibration verified against minor tick marks; extracted low-mass flat level 6.43e-13 and M87 flat level 8.41e-13 reproduce the quoted 6.4e-13 and 8.4e-13. Limit is from stellar axion production in M82 with conversion in IllustrisTNG-analogue magnetic fields (fiducial B-field model, not the stronger SOFIA/HAWC+ variant which would give 3.8e-13); it does not assume axion dark matter, so no density rescaling applied.",
